    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'll try the additive, but I'm worried it's a mechanical failure that won't be fixed by just cleaning it out. It feels almost like something is interfering with the hydraulics at random, like the pressure just jumps for no reason even when everything looks clean. Is there anything else that could cause such sudden, unpredictable behavior in the pressure readings?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
