      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sudden, unpredictable pressure jumps after ruling out fluid and basic solenoids often point to a failing internal filter strainer or a damaged torque converter clutch closure solenoid. A collapsed internal hose or a stuck pressure line can also create erratic readings, while debris from a broken piston could be physically jamming the valve body. Given your concerns about mechanical failure, a comprehensive first-line flush may be insufficient if there is debris clogging the 1-2/2-3 clutches.",
